# pdxdig -- deps.list
#
# Format: one-per-line `<dep> <constraint>` (paideia-os satellite-tool
# convention; mirrors pdxsock/deps.list shape).
#
# pdxdig at v1.3 has no library-external dependencies beyond the SC+
# syscall floor (sysnos 0/1/60 read/write/exit + 115 sys_semantic_send).
# The UDP query path (sendto/recvfrom, sysnos 96/97) is blocked on
# §12.1 and lands at M2-001; libpdx-net will be pulled in as a
# `deps:` entry at that milestone. src/dig_query.pdx (pdxdig#4)
# documents the real `net_resolve` extern contract this dep will
# satisfy but calls nothing outside this repo yet (see that file's
# header on why -- this repo's tools/build.sh links every src/*.o
# into one flat ELF with --fatal-warnings; an unresolved UND symbol
# would break every build, not just the M2-001 call site).
#
# libpdx-audit (pdxdig#7, M3-001) is similarly not yet a real `deps:`
# entry -- src/audit_wire.pdx's `AuditWire::pdxdig_audit_log_query`
# is a WEAK STUB (always returns AFS_OK = 0) called once per accepted
# query from Main::_start; the real body will call
# `AuditFileSink::audit_file_append("/system/audit/pdxdig.log", ...)`
# once this dep lands.
#
# libpdx-argv is not consumed at v1.3 (argv parse is inline in
# src/main.pdx / src/argv_parse.pdx); PDX_TOOL_NAME + PDX_TOOL_VERSION
# externs are provided pre-emptively in src/tool_ident.pdx per the
# libpdx-argv 1.1.3 ENH-032 contract so the eventual bump is a
# one-line manifest edit.

# libpdx-net    >= 0.1.0   # deferred to pdxdig.M2-001 (real UDP query)
# libpdx-audit  >= 0.1.0   # deferred to pdxdig.M3-001-b (real audit_file_append)
# libpdx-argv   >= 1.1.3   # deferred; PDX_TOOL_NAME contract pre-satisfied
